{% comment %}
  ============================================
  DRIFT Theme by WEBEXP, LLC
  Product Badge Snippet
  https://webexp.dev

  Usage: {% render 'drift-badge', product: product %}

  Badge sources (priority order):
  1. Metafield: product.metafields.custom.badge (text) — full override
  2. Product tags: badge:new, badge:limited, badge:sold-out, badge:custom-text
     Tag format: "badge:YOUR TEXT" (case-insensitive prefix match)
  3. Auto sale badge: SAVE XX% when compare_at_price exists
     Controlled by settings.sale_badge_enabled (default: true)

  Output: glassmorphic pill(s) positioned absolute top of parent
  Parent must have position: relative
  ============================================
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign badge_text = ''

  comment
    Priority 1: Metafield override
  endcomment
  if product.metafields.custom.badge != blank
    assign badge_text = product.metafields.custom.badge
  else
    comment
      Priority 2: Product tags — find first "badge:" prefixed tag
    endcomment
    for tag in product.tags
      assign tag_lower = tag | downcase
      if tag_lower contains 'badge:'
        assign badge_text = tag | split: ':' | last | strip
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    Sale badge — auto-calculate SAVE percentage
  endcomment
  assign sale_badge_text = ''
  assign sale_badge_enabled = settings.sale_badge_enabled | default: true
  if sale_badge_enabled and product.compare_at_price_max > product.price_min
    assign save_amount = product.compare_at_price_max | minus: product.price_min
    assign save_pct = save_amount | times: 100 | divided_by: product.compare_at_price_max
    if save_pct > 0
      assign sale_badge_text = 'products.product.sale_badge' | t: percent: save_pct
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Sold-out products show no badges — the "Sold Out" label is already
  on the ATC button / overlay, and a "SAVE %" badge on a sold-out item
  is misleading (the discount isn't available to act on).

  Nested if (Liquid doesn't support parens in boolean expressions —
  `a and (b or c)` causes "Expected dotdot but found comparison").
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product.available -%}
  {%- if badge_text != blank or sale_badge_text != blank -%}
    <span class="drift-badge-stack">
      {%- if badge_text != blank -%}
        <span class="drift-badge" aria-label="Badge: {{ badge_text | escape }}">
          {{ badge_text | escape }}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if sale_badge_text != blank -%}
        <span class="drift-badge drift-badge--sale" aria-label="{{ sale_badge_text }}">
          {{ sale_badge_text }}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}